Two plain-C hook_branchlink wrappers in T2 (Freighter: proj.hook_branchlink("ws_scrn_getres", 0x802D0968); proj.hook_branchlink("ws_scrn_set_stream", 0x802D09DC)):
  void* ws_scrn_getres(const char* n, void* arc){ ws_last_blo = n; return JKRFileLoader_getGlbResource(n, arc); }
  int ws_scrn_set_stream(J2DScreen* s, void* st){ int ok = J2DScreen_set_stream(s, st); if (ok && ws_mode()==2) ws_anchor(s, ws_last_blo); ws_last_blo = 0; return ok; }
ws_anchor: strcmp the name against a small table → rule; root = search(s,'ROOT') ?: s; for each child link: dx = rule(tag, cx); if (dx) J2DPane_add(child, dx, 0); for F-rule children use move+resize. S = (int)(329.5f*(F-1)+0.5f), F from the culling plan's mailbox block (+0xA6C). This covers every J2DScreen in the DOL (57 call sites) and in RELs, so the menus and overlays areas can reuse it by adding table rows.
Alternative (HUD only): hook_branchlink each HUD call site of J2DScreen::set: 0x802051E0 main_parts1, 0x8020529C main_parts2, 0x80205358 main_parts3, 0x80205414 choice_road (all in dMeter_Create 0x80205034), 0x80204208 time_swim_1, 0x80204220 time_swim_2 (dMeter_screenDataTimeSet 0x8020408C), 0x80161034 place_name (dPlace_name_c::setScreen 0x80160F60). Or a single hook at 0x802056C8 (`bl dMeter_screenDataSet` 0x80203464, r3=i_Meter) that walks sMainParts1/2/3 (0x803F7078/7C/80) before calling it.
Keep this in T2: dMeter_Create runs at every stage load, and the first one can come before the REL's 300-frame gate.
